---
import Shell from '../layouts/Shell.astro';
import story from '../../../../kb/research/culture/sounds-website.json';
---
<Shell title={story.title} description={story.lead} active="explore" wide related={false}>
<article class="wrap sounds-story">
<header class="sounds-hero"><div><p class="eyebrow">Living culture · A listening journey</p><h1>Sounds<br/>of <em>Odisha.</em></h1><p class="lead">{story.lead}</p><a class="text-link" href="#huluhuli">Begin with a voice ↓</a></div><figure><img src="/images/sounds/pala-nalconagar.webp" width="1600" height="1200" alt={story.photo.alt} fetchpriority="high"/><figcaption>{story.photo.caption}</figcaption></figure></header>
<p class="sounds-invitation">A sound belongs to an occasion, a place and the people making it. These eight introductions offer a way to begin listening. The opening invitations are imagined scenes; the named accounts are documented sources.</p>
<nav class="sound-chapters" aria-label="Sounds in this collection">{story.chapters.map(c=><a href={'#'+c.id}>{c.name}</a>)}</nav>
{story.chapters.map((c,i)=><section class="sound-chapter" id={c.id}><div class="chapter-heading"><span class="chapter-number" aria-hidden="true">{String(i+1).padStart(2,'0')}</span><p class="eyebrow">{c.name}</p><h2>{c.title}</h2></div><div class="chapter-copy">{c.paragraphs.map(p=><p>{p}</p>)}{c.id==='pala'&&<p><a class="text-link" href="/sounds-of-odisha/pala/">Read the full Pala story →</a></p>}<aside class="sound-question"><h3>A question to carry</h3><p>{c.question}</p></aside></div></section>)}
<section class="listening-care"><p class="eyebrow">Listen with care</p><h2>A visit begins with an invitation.</h2><p>Confirm that an occasion welcomes visitors. Follow the host’s directions and ask separately before photographing, recording or sharing. A ceremony or family gathering does not become a tourist performance because someone arrives with a camera.</p><p>This is a reading collection. Audio recordings are still to come; no current performance or booking is promised.</p><a class="text-link" href="/literature/">Follow voices into Odia literature →</a><p><a href="/contribute/?page=%2Fsounds-of-odisha%2F">Share a public source or suggest a correction</a>. GitHub submissions are public; leave out private contact details and permission documents.</p></section>
<details class="utk-disclosure sound-credits"><summary>Sources, photograph &amp; reading notes</summary><p>{story.limits} Desk review: {story.reviewed_on}.</p>{story.chapters.map(c=><div><h3>{c.name}</h3><ul>{c.source_ids.map(id=>{const s=story.sources.find(s=>s.id===id);return <li><a href={s.resource}>{s.title}</a></li>})}</ul></div>)}<h3>Photograph</h3><p><a href={story.photo.url}>{story.photo.creator} · Pala performance at Nalconagar, 2013</a>. <a href={story.photo.license_url}>{story.photo.license}</a>. {story.photo.changes} The performer is not identified here. No audio licence follows from this photograph’s licence.</p></details>
</article></Shell>
<style>
.sounds-story{padding-bottom:80px}.sounds-hero{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1.15fr;align-items:center;gap:clamp(28px,5vw,100px);padding:50px 0}.sounds-hero h1{font-size:clamp(60px,7vw,128px);line-height:1.02;margin:20px 0 28px}.sounds-hero h1 em{color:var(--sea)}.sounds-hero figure{margin:0}.sounds-hero img{width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:2px}.sounds-hero figcaption{font-size:13px;color:var(--muted);margin-top:12px}.sounds-invitation{max-width:900px;font-size:21px;line-height:1.75}.sound-chapters{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:12px;margin:32px 0 52px}.sound-chapters a{padding:12px 18px;background:var(--paper);border:1px solid var(--line);min-height:44px;color:var(--sea)}.sound-chapter{display:grid;grid-template-columns:.8fr 1.2fr;gap:clamp(28px,7vw,120px);padding:52px 0;border-top:1px solid var(--line);scroll-margin-top:110px}.chapter-number{font-size:50px;color:var(--earth)}.chapter-heading h2{font-size:clamp(32px,3vw,48px);max-width:510px;line-height:1.18}.chapter-copy{max-width:780px;font-size:18px;line-height:1.8}.chapter-copy>p:first-child{margin-top:0}.sound-question{border-left:3px solid var(--sea);background:var(--paper);padding:18px 24px;margin-top:24px}.sound-question h3{font-size:18px;margin:0}.sound-question p{margin:10px 0 0}.listening-care{max-width:950px;margin:35px 0;padding:30px;background:var(--paper);line-height:1.8}.listening-care h2{font-size:36px}.sound-credits{max-width:1000px;overflow-wrap:anywhere}.sound-credits h3{font-size:20px}.sound-credits li{margin:10px 0}@media(max-width:760px){.sounds-hero,.sound-chapter{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:24px}.sounds-hero{padding:28px 0}.sounds-hero h1{font-size:64px}.sound-chapter{padding:32px 0}.chapter-copy{font-size:17px}.listening-care{padding:22px}.listening-care h2{font-size:30px}}
</style>
